From: OpenHands <openhands@all-hands.dev>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 11:31:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] XPU: reset the oneCCL collective chain after each graph-capture warmup (port of #58415, fixed placement)


Port of the unmerged upstream PR #58415 (vllm-project/vllm), corrected for the
dead-code-after-yield bug in that PR (GroupCoordinator.graph_capture is a
generator; code placed after its yield never runs). This variant:
  1. Adds XpuCommunicator.reset_after_graph_capture(): one tiny eager
     all-reduce that replaces the oneCCL chain head event (which a capture
     leaves bound to a command-graph completion event) with an ordinary
     event. No-op when world_size <= 1 or the stream is already capturing.
  2. Calls it from the model-runner capture loop right AFTER the eager
     warmup run and BEFORE the torch.cuda.graph __enter__ (whose
     torch.xpu.synchronize() aborts with UR_RESULT_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST while
     the chain head event is a command-graph one).

Fixes: vllm-project/vllm#58388 (post-capture prefill death) and #60379
(startup death on the first PIECEWISE capture with TP=2 + MTP on a
GDN/Mamba-hybrid model; regression introduced by #56531, which routes
zero-draft rows through the speculative path and thereby into oneCCL
collectives inside the capture window).

Re-hunked onto main @ df417f780a (2026-10-07). Becomes a no-op once upstream
lands #58415 or an equivalent: the call site is a getattr() probe, so if the
method is already provided upstream nothing changes.


diff --git a/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/xpu_communicator.py b/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/xpu_communicator.py
index 7a5913754f..5fcf48b09f 100644
--- a/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/xpu_communicator.py
+++ b/vllm/distributed/device_communicators/xpu_communicator.py
@@ -69,6 +69,29 @@ class XpuCommunicator(DeviceCommunicatorBase):
         dist.all_reduce(output, group=self.device_group)
         return output
 
+    def reset_after_graph_capture(self) -> None:
+        """Issue one tiny eager collective after an XPU graph capture.
+
+        oneCCL chains each collective on the previous one's completion event.
+        After a capture, that event belongs to the captured command graph, and
+        the next (large-message) all-reduce submits with an explicit dependency
+        on it, which makes the submitting queue join the graph's recording.
+        Every later replay/wait then fails with ``xpuStreamCaptureStatus:
+        Recording`` / ``wait cannot be called for a queue which is recording``,
+        and a ``torch.xpu.synchronize()`` at the top of the *next* capture
+        aborts with ``UR_RESULT_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST``. One small eager
+        all-reduce replaces that event with an ordinary one; a later replay
+        never touches oneCCL's host-side state, so doing this once per capture
+        is enough. See upstream #58388 / #58415 and marcinkuk/vllm-2xb50.
+        """
+        if self.world_size <= 1:
+            return
+        _isc = getattr(torch.xpu, "is_current_stream_capturing", None)
+        if _isc is not None and _isc():
+            return
+        flush = torch.zeros(1, dtype=torch.float32, device=self.device)
+        dist.all_reduce(flush, group=self.device_group)
+
     def reduce_scatter(self, input_: torch.Tensor, dim: int = -1):
         world_size = self.world_size
 
diff --git a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py
index 73be62319a..19b7702979 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@ from vllm.config import VllmConfig, set_current_vllm_config
 from vllm.config.compilation import CUDAGraphMode
 from vllm.distributed.parallel_state import (
     get_pp_group,
+    get_tp_group,
     graph_capture,
     is_global_first_rank,
 )
@@ -461,6 +462,20 @@ class CudaGraphManager:
                     # Warmup
                     forward_fn(CUDAGraphMode.NONE)
 
+                    # The warmup above ran an eager forward that issues oneCCL
+                    # collectives, leaving the XPU queue's completion event
+                    # bound to oneCCL's chain (the event of the last collective,
+                    # which may still be attached to a graph). The capture's
+                    # torch.cuda.graph __enter__ calls torch.xpu.synchronize(),
+                    # which faults with UR_RESULT_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST while that
+                    # event is a command-graph one. One tiny eager all-reduce
+                    # replaces it with an ordinary event. XPU-only, no-op when
+                    # not multi-GPU or mid-capture.
+                    _dc = getattr(get_tp_group(), "device_communicator", None)
+                    _reset = getattr(_dc, "reset_after_graph_capture", None)
+                    if _reset is not None:
+                        _reset()
+
                     # Capture
                     logger.debug(
                         "CG Capture: mode=%s, batch_desc=%s",
